"""Paragraph descriptions for GameRuleEnv facts.
Each entry maps a question to a paragraph with the answer appearing early."""

EASY_PARAGRAPHS = {
    "How many pieces does each player start with in chess?": "Each player starts with 16 pieces in chess, arranged on the two ranks closest to them. The pieces consist of one king, one queen, two rooks, two bishops, two knights, and eight pawns. The arrangement is symmetrical, with both players having identical sets of pieces in opposing colors.",
    "How many squares are on a standard chessboard?": "A standard chessboard has 64 squares, arranged in an 8 by 8 grid of alternating light and dark colors. The board is positioned so that each player has a light-colored square in the near-right corner. The squares are labeled using algebraic notation with columns lettered a through h and rows numbered 1 through 8.",
    "How many cards are in a standard deck (no jokers)?": "A standard deck contains 52 cards, divided equally among four suits: hearts, diamonds, clubs, and spades. Each suit contains 13 cards ranging from ace through 10, plus three face cards: jack, queen, and king. Most commercially produced decks also include two joker cards, but the standard playing deck excludes them.",
    "How many tiles are used in a standard Scrabble game?": "A standard Scrabble game uses 100 tiles in total, including 98 letter tiles and 2 blank tiles that can represent any letter. The letter distribution is weighted by frequency in English, with common letters like E having 12 tiles and rare letters like Z having only one. Players draw seven tiles each from a bag at the start of the game.",
    "How many dots are on a standard six-sided die total?": "A standard six-sided die has 21 dots in total, distributed across its six faces showing 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6 pips respectively. Opposite faces of a standard die always sum to 7. Dice have been used as randomizers in games for thousands of years, with examples found in ancient Egyptian and Mesopotamian archaeological sites.",
    "How many pieces are in a standard dominoes set (double-six)?": "A standard double-six dominoes set contains 28 pieces, each displaying two groups of spots representing values from 0 to 6. Every possible combination of two values appears exactly once in the set. Dominoes originated in China during the 12th century and were introduced to Europe in the 18th century.",
    "How many red properties are on a Monopoly board?": "There are 3 red properties on a standard Monopoly board: Kentucky Avenue, Indiana Avenue, and Illinois Avenue. The red color group is located on the third side of the board and is one of the most frequently landed-upon property groups in the game. Illinois Avenue is statistically the single most landed-on property in standard Monopoly.",
    "How many spaces are on a standard Monopoly board?": "A standard Monopoly board has 40 spaces arranged around the perimeter of the board. These include 28 properties grouped into color sets, 4 railroad spaces, 2 utility spaces, and several special spaces including Go, Jail, Free Parking, and Go to Jail. Players move clockwise around the board based on dice rolls.",
    "How many pawns does each player start with in chess?": "Each player starts with 8 pawns in chess, positioned in a row on the second rank from the player's perspective. Pawns are the most numerous piece and can only move forward, one square at a time, except on their first move when they may advance two squares. Despite being the least powerful piece, pawns play a critical role in controlling the center and can be promoted upon reaching the opposite end of the board.",
    "How many suits are in a standard deck of cards?": "A standard deck of cards contains 4 suits: hearts, diamonds, clubs, and spades. Hearts and diamonds are red suits, while clubs and spades are black suits. Each suit contains exactly 13 cards, giving the deck its total of 52 cards. The four-suit system has been standard in most Western card games since the 15th century.",
    "How many black squares are on a standard chessboard?": "A standard chessboard has 32 black squares (or dark-colored squares), making up exactly half of the 64 total squares on the board. The remaining 32 squares are white or light-colored. Bishops are restricted to squares of one color throughout the game, which is why each player starts with one bishop on light squares and one on dark.",
    "How many points is the letter Q worth in Scrabble?": "The letter Q is worth 10 points in Scrabble, making it one of the two highest-valued tiles alongside Z. There is only one Q tile in the standard English Scrabble set. The high point value reflects the letter's rarity in English and the difficulty of using it, as Q almost always requires a U to form valid words.",
    "How many letters are drawn at the start of a Scrabble game per player?": "Each player draws 7 letters at the start of a Scrabble game from a bag containing 100 tiles. Players maintain a rack of 7 tiles throughout the game, drawing replacements after each turn. The first player to place a word must cover the center star square on the board.",
    "How many cells are in a standard 9x9 Sudoku grid?": "A standard 9x9 Sudoku grid contains 81 cells arranged in 9 rows and 9 columns. The grid is further divided into nine 3x3 subgrids called boxes or regions. The objective is to fill every cell with a digit from 1 to 9 such that each row, column, and box contains all nine digits without repetition.",
    "How many regions are in a standard 9x9 Sudoku grid?": "A standard 9x9 Sudoku grid is divided into 9 regions, also called boxes or blocks, each containing a 3x3 arrangement of cells. In a valid solution, each region must contain the digits 1 through 9 exactly once. The regions are typically delineated by thicker lines or borders within the grid.",
    "How many face cards are in a standard deck of cards?": "A standard deck of cards contains 12 face cards in total, consisting of four jacks, four queens, and four kings, one of each in every suit. Face cards are also known as court cards. In most card games, face cards have specific values; for example, in Blackjack, all face cards are valued at 10.",
    "How many aces are in a standard deck of cards?": "A standard deck of cards contains 4 aces, one in each of the four suits: hearts, diamonds, clubs, and spades. The ace is unique in many card games because it can serve as either the highest or lowest card depending on the rules. In Blackjack, an ace can count as either 1 or 11.",
    "How many Community Chest cards are in standard Monopoly?": "There are 16 Community Chest cards in standard Monopoly, placed in a deck on the board. Players draw a Community Chest card when they land on a Community Chest space. The cards contain various instructions such as collecting bank errors in your favor, paying doctor's fees, or advancing to Go.",
    "How many Chance cards are in standard Monopoly?": "There are 16 Chance cards in standard Monopoly, forming a separate deck from the Community Chest cards. Chance cards are drawn when a player lands on a Chance space and typically involve movement to other board locations or financial transactions. Some of the most impactful Chance cards direct players to advance to Boardwalk or go directly to Jail.",
    "How many pins are used in a standard game of ten-pin bowling?": "A standard game of ten-pin bowling uses 10 pins arranged in a triangular formation at the end of the lane. The pins are set in four rows: one pin in the front, two in the second row, three in the third, and four in the back row. Each pin stands 15 inches tall and weighs between 3 pounds 6 ounces and 3 pounds 10 ounces.",
    "How many holes are in a standard round of golf?": "A standard round of golf consists of 18 holes, played in sequence on a golf course. Most courses are divided into a front nine and a back nine. The concept of 18 holes became standard at the Old Course at St Andrews in Scotland, which has been the home of golf since the 15th century.",
    "How many players are on a standard basketball team on the court?": "A standard basketball team has 5 players on the court at any given time, though rosters typically include additional substitutes. The five positions are point guard, shooting guard, small forward, power forward, and center. Basketball was invented by James Naismith in 1891 and has grown into one of the world's most popular sports.",
    "How many players are on a standard soccer team on the field?": "A standard soccer team has 11 players on the field, including one goalkeeper and ten outfield players. Teams can name a number of substitutes on the bench, with most professional competitions allowing three to five substitutions per match. Soccer, known as football outside North America, is the world's most popular sport.",
    "How many players are on a standard volleyball team on the court?": "A standard volleyball team has 6 players on the court at any given time, arranged in two rows of three. Players rotate positions clockwise each time their team wins the serve. The sport was invented in 1895 by William G. Morgan and has been an Olympic sport since 1964.",
    "How many points is a touchdown worth in American football?": "A touchdown is worth 6 points in American football, scored when a player carries the ball into or catches it in the opposing team's end zone. Following a touchdown, the scoring team has the option to attempt an extra point kick worth 1 point or a two-point conversion. The touchdown is the primary scoring method in the sport.",
    "How many periods are in a standard ice hockey game?": "A standard ice hockey game consists of 3 periods, each lasting 20 minutes of play time. If the game is tied after three periods in regular season play, an overtime period and potentially a shootout are used to determine the winner. The three-period format has been standard in professional hockey since the early days of the NHL.",
    "How many bases are on a baseball diamond?": "A baseball diamond has 4 bases: first base, second base, third base, and home plate. The bases are arranged in a square with 90 feet between each base in professional baseball. A player who successfully touches all four bases in order scores a run for their team.",
    "How many players are on a baseball team on the field?": "A baseball team has 9 players on the field during defensive play, each assigned to a specific position. The positions are pitcher, catcher, first baseman, second baseman, third baseman, shortstop, left fielder, center fielder, and right fielder. In the American League, a designated hitter bats in place of the pitcher.",
    "How many points is the bullseye worth in standard darts?": "The bullseye is worth 50 points in standard darts, representing the highest single-dart score on the board. The bullseye is divided into two sections: the inner bull (worth 50 points) and the outer bull (worth 25 points). However, the maximum single-dart score achievable on the board is actually 60, scored by hitting the triple-20 segment.",
    "How many squares are in a standard Snakes and Ladders board?": "A standard Snakes and Ladders board contains 100 squares, numbered from 1 to 100 in a winding path from the bottom-left corner to the top. The game originated in ancient India, where it was known as Moksha Patam and was designed as a moral instruction tool. Players advance by rolling dice and encounter snakes that send them backward or ladders that move them forward.",
    "How many knights does each chess player start with?": "Each chess player starts with 2 knights, placed between the rooks and bishops on the back rank. Knights have a unique L-shaped movement pattern, jumping two squares in one direction and one square perpendicular to that. They are the only pieces that can jump over other pieces, making them particularly valuable in crowded positions.",
    "How many bishops does each chess player start with?": "Each chess player starts with 2 bishops, one positioned on a light square and one on a dark square. Bishops move diagonally any number of squares and are confined to squares of one color for the entire game. The two bishops working together can control both colors and are considered slightly more valuable than two knights in open positions.",
    "How many rooks does each chess player start with?": "Each chess player starts with 2 rooks, placed in the corners of the board on the first rank. Rooks move horizontally or vertically any number of squares and are considered the second most powerful piece after the queen. They play a crucial role in the special move known as castling, where the king and a rook move simultaneously.",
    "How many queens does each chess player start with?": "Each chess player starts with 1 queen, placed on the square of its own color on the first rank next to the king. The queen is the most powerful piece in chess, combining the movement abilities of both the rook and bishop. Losing the queen early in a game is typically a decisive disadvantage.",
    "How many frames are in a standard game of bowling?": "A standard game of bowling consists of 10 frames, with each frame giving the player up to two attempts to knock down all ten pins. If a player knocks down all pins on the first ball, it is called a strike. The tenth frame has special rules allowing up to three balls if the player achieves a strike or spare.",
    "How many points is a field goal worth in American football?": "A field goal is worth 3 points in American football, scored when a player kicks the ball through the opponent's goalposts from the field of play. Field goals are typically attempted on fourth down when the team is within kicking range but unlikely to score a touchdown. The longest field goal in NFL history is 66 yards.",
    "How many players are on a standard cricket team on the field?": "A standard cricket team has 11 players on the field, with roles including batsmen, bowlers, and fielders. The fielding side has all eleven players on the field, while the batting side has two batsmen at the wicket at any time. Cricket originated in England and is now one of the most popular sports in Commonwealth nations.",
    "How many sets are needed to win a standard men's tennis Grand Slam match?": "A player needs to win 3 sets to win a standard men's Grand Slam tennis match, as men's singles at Grand Slam tournaments are played as best-of-five-set matches. Each set is won by the first player to reach six games with a margin of at least two. A tiebreak is played when the set reaches 6-6 in most situations.",
    "How many pockets are on a standard pool table?": "A standard pool table has 6 pockets: one in each of the four corners and one at the midpoint of each long side. The pockets are designed to catch balls that are directed into them by the cue ball. Different variations of pool, such as 8-ball and 9-ball, use the same table configuration but have different rules for gameplay.",
    "How many balls are used in a standard game of pool (8-ball)?": "A standard game of 8-ball pool uses 16 balls in total: one white cue ball and fifteen numbered object balls. The object balls consist of seven solid-colored balls numbered 1 through 7, seven striped balls numbered 9 through 15, and the black 8-ball. Players are assigned either solids or stripes and must pocket all their balls before legally pocketing the 8-ball to win.",
    "How many cards does each player get in a standard poker hand?": "Each player receives 5 cards in a standard poker hand, such as in five-card draw. Hand rankings from highest to lowest are: royal flush, straight flush, four of a kind, full house, flush, straight, three of a kind, two pair, one pair, and high card. In popular variants like Texas Hold'em, players receive only two private cards and share five community cards.",
    "How many cards does each player start with in standard Blackjack?": "Each player starts with 2 cards in standard Blackjack, as does the dealer. One of the dealer's cards is dealt face up and the other face down, known as the hole card. The goal is to get a hand total as close to 21 as possible without going over, with face cards worth 10 and aces worth 1 or 11.",
    "How many quarters are in a standard basketball game?": "A standard basketball game consists of 4 quarters. In the NBA, each quarter lasts 12 minutes, while college basketball uses two 20-minute halves. If the score is tied at the end of regulation, a five-minute overtime period is played, with additional overtimes as needed until a winner is determined.",
    "How many periods are in a standard hockey game?": "A standard hockey game is divided into 3 periods, each consisting of 20 minutes of playing time. Between periods, the ice surface is resurfaced by a Zamboni machine. If the game remains tied after three periods during the regular season, teams play a five-minute sudden-death overtime followed by a shootout if necessary.",
    "How many innings are in a standard baseball game?": "A standard baseball game consists of 9 innings, with each inning divided into a top half and a bottom half. The visiting team bats in the top of each inning and the home team bats in the bottom. If the game is tied after nine innings, extra innings are played until one team has more runs at the end of a complete inning.",
    "How many sets are played in a standard tennis match (men's Grand Slam)?": "Men's Grand Slam tennis matches are played as best of 5 sets, meaning a player must win three sets to win the match. Each set is played until one player wins six games with a two-game lead, or through a tiebreak at 6-6. Grand Slam tournaments are the four most prestigious events in tennis: the Australian Open, French Open, Wimbledon, and the US Open.",
    "How many players are on a standard cricket team?": "A standard cricket team consists of 11 players, selected from a larger squad for each match. The team includes specialist batsmen, bowlers, all-rounders who can both bat and bowl, and a wicket-keeper who stands behind the stumps. The captain selects the batting order and makes strategic bowling and fielding decisions throughout the match.",
    "How many players are on a standard rugby union team?": "A standard rugby union team has 15 players on the field, divided into eight forwards and seven backs. The forwards are primarily responsible for winning possession through scrums, lineouts, and rucks, while the backs focus on running with the ball and scoring tries. Up to eight substitutes can be used during a match in international rugby.",
    "How many wickets does each side have in a cricket innings?": "Each side has 10 wickets in a cricket innings, meaning the batting team's innings ends when ten of its eleven batsmen are dismissed. The eleventh batsman is considered not out since there is no partner to bat with. A team can also choose to declare their innings closed before losing all ten wickets if they believe they have scored enough runs.",
    "How many red balls are on a standard snooker table?": "A standard snooker table has 15 red balls at the start of each frame, arranged in a triangular formation near the bottom end of the table. Red balls are each worth one point and must be potted alternately with colored balls during play. Once all reds have been potted, the six colored balls are potted in ascending order of their point values.",
    "How many total balls are on a standard snooker table at the start?": "A standard snooker table has 22 balls at the start of a frame: 15 red balls, 6 colored balls (yellow, green, brown, blue, pink, and black), and 1 white cue ball. The colored balls have point values ranging from 2 for yellow to 7 for black. The maximum possible break in a single frame is 147, achieved by potting all reds with blacks followed by all colors.",
    "How many pockets does a standard pool table have?": "A standard pool table has 6 pockets positioned at the four corners and at the midpoints of the two longer sides. The pockets are slightly larger than the balls to allow for some margin of error when shooting. Professional tournament tables typically have tighter pocket openings than recreational tables, increasing the difficulty of the game.",
    "How many lanes are in a standard Olympic swimming pool?": "A standard Olympic swimming pool has 8 lanes, each 2.5 meters wide. The pool is 50 meters long and at least 2 meters deep. Lane assignments for races are determined by qualifying times, with the fastest qualifiers placed in the center lanes, which are considered advantageous because of reduced wave interference from the pool walls.",
    "How many hurdles are in a standard 110m hurdles race?": "A standard 110-meter hurdles race features 10 hurdles spaced at regular intervals along the track. The hurdles are set at a height of 1.067 meters (3 feet 6 inches) for men's competitions. The first hurdle is placed 13.72 meters from the starting line, with subsequent hurdles 9.14 meters apart, and the final hurdle 14.02 meters from the finish.",
    "How many points is a try worth in rugby union?": "A try is worth 5 points in rugby union, scored when a player grounds the ball in the opposing team's in-goal area. After scoring a try, the scoring team is awarded a conversion kick worth an additional 2 points. A penalty goal or drop goal during open play is worth 3 points. The try has been worth 5 points since 1992, having been previously valued at 4 points.",
    "How many overs are in a standard cricket One Day International match per side?": "Each side bowls 50 overs in a standard cricket One Day International (ODI) match. Each over consists of six legal deliveries bowled by a single bowler. The format was introduced in the 1970s as a shorter alternative to multi-day Test cricket and has been a staple of international cricket ever since, with the Cricket World Cup being contested in this format.",
    "How many players are on a standard water polo team in the water?": "A standard water polo team has 7 players in the water at any given time, including one goalkeeper. Teams can have up to six substitutes available on the bench. The game is played in four periods of eight minutes each, and players must tread water throughout the match as they are not allowed to touch the bottom of the pool.",
    "How many doubles are needed to finish a game of darts (standard 501)?": "Exactly 1 double is needed to finish a game of standard 501 darts, as the rules require the final dart to land in a double segment or the bullseye to win. Players start with 501 points and subtract each score until they reach exactly zero. If a player's remaining score goes below zero or to exactly one (which cannot be finished with a double), the turn is voided.",
    "How many points is the bullseye worth in darts?": "The bullseye is worth 50 points in darts, representing the center of the dartboard. The bullseye is divided into two sections: the inner bull (the very center, worth 50 points and counting as a double for checkout purposes) and the outer bull (the ring surrounding it, worth 25 points). Despite its central location, the triple-20 segment scores more at 60 points.",
    "How many tiles does each player draw at the start of a standard Dominoes game?": "Each player draws 7 tiles at the start of a standard Dominoes game when playing with two, three, or four players. The remaining tiles are placed aside as the boneyard and can be drawn from during the game. In variants with more players, fewer tiles may be drawn initially. The double-six set of 28 tiles is the most commonly used.",
    "How many marbles does each player start with in Chinese Checkers?": "Each player starts with 10 marbles in Chinese Checkers, placed in one of the six pointed triangular extensions of the star-shaped board. Despite its name, the game was invented in Germany in 1892, not in China. Players move their marbles across the board by single steps or by jumping over other marbles, aiming to be the first to move all their pieces to the opposite triangle.",
    "How many stones does each player start with in Go (standard game)?": "Each player starts with 0 stones on the board in Go, as the game begins with an empty board and players place stones one at a time during their turns. Black traditionally plays first, placing a stone on any intersection of the 19x19 grid. The game provides an unlimited supply of stones, with 181 black stones and 180 white stones in a standard set, far more than are typically used in a single game.",
    "How many total dominoes are in a standard double-six set?": "A standard double-six domino set contains 28 tiles in total. Each tile displays two groups of dots representing all possible pairings of values from zero (blank) to six. The number of tiles in a double-n set follows the formula (n+1)(n+2)/2, which gives 28 for n=6. Larger sets such as double-nine (55 tiles) and double-twelve (91 tiles) are also commonly available.",
    "How many numbered cards are in a standard Uno deck?": "A standard Uno deck contains 76 numbered cards, distributed across four colors: red, yellow, green, and blue. Each color has cards numbered 0 through 9, with one zero card and two of each number 1 through 9 per color. The full Uno deck of 108 cards also includes action cards (Skip, Reverse, Draw Two) and Wild cards.",
    "How many wild cards are in a standard Uno deck?": "A standard Uno deck contains 8 wild cards, consisting of four regular Wild cards and four Wild Draw Four cards. Wild cards can be played on any turn regardless of the current color or number, and the player who plays one chooses the next color. Wild Draw Four cards additionally force the next player to draw four cards and skip their turn.",
    "How many pieces does each player have in standard Checkers?": "Each player starts with 12 pieces in standard Checkers, placed on the dark squares of the three rows closest to their side of the board. Pieces can only move diagonally forward on dark squares and capture opposing pieces by jumping over them. When a piece reaches the opposite end of the board, it is crowned and becomes a king, gaining the ability to move backward.",
    "How many squares are on a standard Checkers board?": "A standard Checkers board has 64 squares in total, arranged in an 8x8 grid of alternating light and dark colors, identical to a chess board. However, only the 32 dark squares are used in gameplay, as pieces move exclusively on dark-colored squares. The board is oriented so that each player has a dark square in the left corner of the row nearest to them.",
    "How many points is a safety worth in American football?": "A safety is worth 2 points in American football and is one of the rarest scoring plays in the game. A safety is awarded to the defensive team when the ball carrier is tackled, goes out of bounds, or commits certain penalties in their own end zone. Following a safety, the team that was scored upon must also kick the ball to the scoring team.",
    "How many players are on a standard lacrosse team on the field?": "A standard lacrosse team has 10 players on the field in men's field lacrosse, consisting of three attackmen, three midfielders, three defensemen, and one goalkeeper. Women's lacrosse features 12 players per side. The sport originated among Native American communities and is one of the oldest team sports in North America.",
    "How many chukkers are in a standard polo match?": "A standard polo match consists of 6 chukkers (also spelled chukkas), each lasting seven and a half minutes of playing time. Players typically change horses between chukkers because of the physical demands placed on the animals. Polo is one of the oldest known team sports, with origins dating back over 2,500 years to Central Asian civilizations.",
    "How many ends are in a standard curling match?": "A standard curling match consists of 10 ends, which function similarly to innings in baseball. In each end, both teams deliver eight stones alternately toward the target area called the house. The team with the stone closest to the center of the house after all stones are delivered scores points for that end.",
    "How many players are on a standard field hockey team on the field?": "A standard field hockey team has 11 players on the field, including one goalkeeper and ten outfield players. Substitutions are unlimited and can be made at any time during play. Field hockey is one of the oldest known ball-and-stick games, with evidence of similar games played in ancient Egypt, Greece, and Rome.",
}

MEDIUM_PARAGRAPHS = {
    "How many total possible opening moves are there in chess for White?": "White has 20 total possible opening moves in chess: each of the eight pawns can move one or two squares forward (giving 16 pawn moves), and each of the two knights can move to two different squares (giving 4 knight moves). No other pieces can move on the first turn because they are blocked by the pawns. This gives the first player a significant choice that shapes the entire direction of the game.",
    "How many tiles are in a standard Mahjong set?": "A standard Mahjong set contains 144 tiles, comprising 36 character tiles, 36 bamboo tiles, 36 circle tiles, 16 wind tiles, 12 dragon tiles, and 8 bonus tiles (4 flowers and 4 seasons). The game originated in China during the Qing dynasty and involves players drawing and discarding tiles to form specific combinations. Regional variants may use slightly different tile sets.",
    "How many playable intersections are on a standard Go board (19x19)?": "A standard Go board has 361 playable intersections, formed by a grid of 19 horizontal and 19 vertical lines. Players place stones on these intersections rather than inside the squares. The 19x19 board is used for professional and tournament play, while smaller 9x9 and 13x13 boards are common for beginners and shorter games.",
    "How many unique two-card starting hands exist in Texas Hold'em poker?": "There are 1326 unique two-card starting hands in Texas Hold'em poker, calculated as the combination of 52 cards taken 2 at a time. However, when considering that suits are interchangeable for unpaired hands, there are only 169 strategically distinct starting hands. The strongest starting hand is a pair of aces, while the weakest is generally considered to be 7-2 offsuit.",
    "How many total dominoes are in a double-nine set?": "A double-nine domino set contains 55 tiles, covering all possible pairings of values from zero through nine. This is significantly larger than the standard double-six set of 28 tiles and allows for more players and more complex games. The number of tiles in any double-n set follows the triangular number formula (n+1)(n+2)/2.",
    "How many letter tiles have zero point value in Scrabble (blanks)?": "Scrabble includes 2 blank tiles that have zero point value and can represent any letter of the alphabet. Blank tiles are among the most valuable tiles in the game despite scoring no points themselves because of their flexibility in forming high-scoring words. Once a blank is placed on the board and designated as a specific letter, it remains that letter for the rest of the game.",
    "How many railroad spaces are on a standard Monopoly board?": "A standard Monopoly board has 4 railroad spaces: Reading Railroad, Pennsylvania Railroad, B&O Railroad, and Short Line. Each railroad costs $200 to purchase, and the rent increases with each additional railroad owned by the same player, from $25 for one up to $200 for all four. Railroads are among the most profitable investments in Monopoly relative to their cost.",
    "How many property groups (color sets) are in standard Monopoly?": "Standard Monopoly has 8 property groups organized by color: brown (dark purple), light blue, pink, orange, red, yellow, green, and dark blue. Each color group contains two or three properties that must all be owned by the same player before houses and hotels can be built. The orange properties are statistically the most profitable due to their proximity to the Jail square.",
    "How many cards does each player receive in a standard game of Bridge?": "Each player receives 13 cards in a standard game of Bridge, as the entire 52-card deck is dealt equally among four players. Players are seated in two partnerships opposite each other, and the game involves bidding for contracts and then playing the hand. Bridge is considered one of the most complex and strategic card games.",
    "How many discs does each player start with in Othello (Reversi)?": "Each player starts with 2 discs in Othello, placed in the center of the 8x8 board in a diagonal pattern with alternating colors. The discs are two-sided, with one black and one white face. Players take turns placing discs to outflank and flip their opponent's pieces. The player with the most discs of their color when the board is full wins.",
    "How many pieces does each player have in Backgammon?": "Each player has 15 pieces (called checkers or stones) in Backgammon, distributed across specific points on the board at the start of the game. Players roll dice and move their checkers around the board in opposite directions, aiming to bear off all their pieces before their opponent. Backgammon is one of the oldest known board games, with origins dating back approximately 5,000 years.",
    "How many points are on a standard Backgammon board?": "A standard Backgammon board has 24 points (narrow triangles) arranged in four quadrants of six points each. The points are alternately colored and are numbered 1 through 24, with each player counting from opposite ends of the board. The bar in the center divides the board into the home and outer boards for each player.",
    "How many territory cards are in the board game Risk?": "The board game Risk contains 42 territory cards, one for each territory on the board. Each card shows the territory name and one of three symbols: infantry, cavalry, or artillery. Players receive territory cards for conquering at least one territory during their turn and can trade in matching sets for bonus armies.",
    "How many hexagonal tiles are in the base Catan board?": "The base Catan board consists of 19 hexagonal tiles arranged in a roughly circular pattern. These include one desert tile that produces no resources and 18 resource-producing tiles: 4 forests (lumber), 4 pastures (wool), 4 fields (grain), 3 hills (brick), and 3 mountains (ore). The tiles are arranged randomly at the start of each game to create a unique board.",
    "How many resource types are in the base Settlers of Catan?": "The base Settlers of Catan features 5 resource types: lumber, wool, grain, brick, and ore. Players collect these resources based on the placement of their settlements and cities adjacent to hexagonal terrain tiles. Different combinations of resources are needed to build roads, settlements, cities, and development cards, requiring players to trade with each other to acquire what they need.",
    "How many letter S tiles are in a standard English Scrabble set?": "A standard English Scrabble set contains 4 letter S tiles, each worth one point. The S tile is highly valuable strategically because it can be added to the end of existing words on the board to form plurals, simultaneously creating a new word. Experienced players often save S tiles for high-scoring opportunities rather than using them in routine plays.",
    "How many cards are in a standard Uno deck?": "A standard Uno deck contains 108 cards in total, comprising numbered cards (0-9) in four colors, action cards (Skip, Reverse, Draw Two in each color), and wild cards. The game was created in 1971 by Merle Robbins and has become one of the best-selling card games in the world. Players aim to be the first to empty their hand by matching cards by color or number.",
    "How many maximum points can be scored in a single turn in Yahtzee?": "The maximum points that can be scored in a single turn in Yahtzee is 50, achieved by rolling five of a kind (a Yahtzee). If a player rolls a Yahtzee and the Yahtzee category has already been scored, bonus Yahtzees are worth 100 additional points each, but only if the player's corresponding upper section box has been filled. Yahtzee is a dice game played with five dice.",
    "How many categories are scored in a standard Yahtzee game?": "A standard Yahtzee game has 13 scoring categories that must each be filled exactly once during the game. The upper section has six categories (Ones through Sixes) that sum specific die values, while the lower section has seven categories including Three of a Kind, Four of a Kind, Full House, Small Straight, Large Straight, Chance, and Yahtzee.",
    "How many total squares can be found on a chessboard (all sizes)?": "A chessboard contains 204 total squares when counting squares of all possible sizes. This includes 64 individual 1x1 squares, 49 squares of size 2x2, 36 of size 3x3, 25 of size 4x4, 16 of size 5x5, 9 of size 6x6, 4 of size 7x7, and 1 square of size 8x8. The calculation follows the sum of squares formula: the sum of n-squared from 1 to 8.",
    "How many unique ways can the first four moves of chess be played?": "There are 71852 unique ways the first four moves of chess can be played, counting two moves by each player (four half-moves total). After White's first move (20 options) and Black's response (20 options), each side has an increasing number of possibilities based on piece development. This rapid expansion of possibilities is one reason chess has never been computationally solved.",
    "How many dice are used in a game of Yahtzee?": "Yahtzee is played with 5 dice, which players roll up to three times per turn to achieve specific combinations. After the first roll, the player may set aside any dice and re-roll the remaining ones. After three rolls, or when the player is satisfied, the result must be recorded in one of the thirteen scoring categories on the scorecard.",
    "How many rooms are in the board game Clue (Cluedo)?": "The board game Clue contains 9 rooms where the fictional murder may have taken place: the Kitchen, Ballroom, Conservatory, Billiard Room, Library, Study, Hall, Lounge, and Dining Room. Players move between rooms to make suggestions about the murder suspect, weapon, and room. The game was first published in 1949 in the United Kingdom under the name Cluedo.",
    "How many suspect characters are in the board game Clue (Cluedo)?": "The board game Clue features 6 suspect characters: Miss Scarlet, Colonel Mustard, Mrs. White, Reverend Green, Mrs. Peacock, and Professor Plum. Each player takes on the role of one suspect and moves around the board to gather clues. The objective is to deduce which suspect committed the murder, with which weapon, and in which room.",
    "How many weapon cards are in the board game Clue (Cluedo)?": "The board game Clue contains 6 weapon cards corresponding to six miniature weapon tokens: the candlestick, knife, lead pipe, revolver, rope, and wrench. One weapon card is placed in the confidential case file along with one suspect and one room card to form the solution. Players eliminate possibilities through the process of making suggestions and receiving cards from other players.",
    "How many letter E tiles are in a standard English Scrabble set?": "A standard English Scrabble set contains 12 letter E tiles, making E the most abundant letter in the game. Each E tile is worth only one point, reflecting the letter's high frequency in English. The large number of E tiles means they are commonly available for rack balancing, though having too many can be a disadvantage since they limit high-scoring consonant combinations.",
    "How many victory points do you need to win base Catan?": "A player needs 10 victory points to win the base game of Settlers of Catan. Points can be earned through building settlements (1 point each), upgrading to cities (2 points each), holding the Longest Road card (2 points), holding the Largest Army card (2 points), and through certain development cards that award 1 victory point each.",
    "How many harbors are on the standard Catan board?": "The standard Catan board features 9 harbors placed around the coastline of the island. Five of these are generic 3-for-1 harbors that allow trading any three of one resource for one of any other. The remaining four are specialized 2-for-1 harbors, each dedicated to a specific resource type, providing a more favorable trading ratio.",
    "How many development cards are in base Catan?": "The base game of Settlers of Catan includes 25 development cards that players can purchase for specific resource combinations. The development deck consists of 14 Knight cards, 5 Victory Point cards, 2 Road Building cards, 2 Monopoly cards, and 2 Year of Plenty cards. Development cards provide various strategic advantages and are drawn face-down from a shuffled pile.",
    "How many knight cards are in a base Catan development deck?": "A base Catan development deck contains 14 Knight cards, making them the most common development card type. Playing a Knight card allows the player to move the robber to a new hex and steal a resource from an adjacent player. Accumulating three or more Knights earns the Largest Army bonus worth 2 victory points, which is contested throughout the game.",
    "How many stones does Black place first in a game of Go?": "Black places 1 stone first in a game of Go, as the game begins with an empty board and Black always moves first. This first-move advantage is traditionally compensated by a scoring bonus called komi given to White, typically 6.5 or 7.5 points in modern rules. Go is considered one of the most complex board games, with more possible positions than atoms in the observable universe.",
    "How many life points does each player start with in standard Magic: The Gathering?": "Each player starts with 20 life points in standard Magic: The Gathering, and the primary way to win is to reduce your opponent's life total to zero. Players can also win by forcing their opponent to draw from an empty library or through special card abilities that state alternative win conditions. Magic was created by Richard Garfield and first published in 1993, becoming the world's first trading card game.",
    "How many cards are in a standard Tarot deck?": "A standard Tarot deck contains 78 cards, divided into two main groups. The Major Arcana consists of 22 cards representing significant life events and archetypes, while the Minor Arcana contains 56 cards divided into four suits of 14 cards each. Although commonly associated with divination, Tarot cards were originally designed for playing card games in 15th-century Europe.",
    "How many Major Arcana cards are in a Tarot deck?": "A Tarot deck contains 22 Major Arcana cards, numbered from 0 (The Fool) through 21 (The World). These cards depict significant archetypes and life themes such as The Magician, The High Priestess, The Empress, The Tower, and Death. In Tarot readings, Major Arcana cards are considered to carry greater significance than the 56 Minor Arcana cards.",
    "How many tiles are in a standard set of Rummikub?": "A standard Rummikub set contains 106 tiles: 104 numbered tiles in four colors (two sets of tiles numbered 1 through 13 in each of black, blue, orange, and red) plus 2 joker tiles. Players arrange tiles into runs of consecutive numbers in the same color or groups of the same number in different colors. The game was invented by Ephraim Hertzano in the 1940s.",
    "How many letter Z tiles are in a standard English Scrabble set?": "There is 1 letter Z tile in a standard English Scrabble set, and it is worth 10 points, tied with Q as the highest-valued tile. The single Z tile reflects the letter's rarity in English. Despite its scarcity, the Z tile can be very valuable when played on bonus squares, particularly triple-letter or triple-word score positions.",
    "How many bonus squares are on a standard Scrabble board?": "A standard Scrabble board features 60 bonus squares distributed across the 15x15 grid. These include 24 double-letter score squares, 17 double-word score squares, 12 triple-letter score squares, and 8 triple-word score squares (including the center star, which counts as a double-word square). Strategic placement on these squares can dramatically increase a player's score.",
    "How many double word score squares are on a Scrabble board?": "A Scrabble board has 17 double word score squares, shown in light pink on standard boards. These include the center star square, which serves as both the starting position and a double-word square, and 16 additional squares arranged in diagonal lines radiating from the center. Landing on a double-word score square doubles the total value of all tiles in that word.",
    "How many triple word score squares are on a Scrabble board?": "A Scrabble board contains 8 triple word score squares, typically shown in dark red on standard boards. These squares are positioned at regular intervals around the edges of the board and in the four corners. Landing on a triple-word square triples the entire value of the word placed there, making these the most coveted positions for high-scoring plays.",
    "How many total rectangles can be found on a chessboard?": "A chessboard contains 1296 total rectangles when counting all possible rectangles of every size and orientation. This is calculated by choosing two horizontal lines and two vertical lines from the nine lines that form the grid, giving C(9,2) x C(9,2) = 36 x 36 = 1296. This count includes the 204 squares, since squares are a special case of rectangles.",
    "How many dominoes are in a double-twelve set?": "A double-twelve domino set contains 91 tiles, covering all possible pairings of values from zero (blank) through twelve. This makes it significantly larger than the standard double-six set (28 tiles) or the double-nine set (55 tiles). Double-twelve sets are popular for games with larger groups of players, as the additional tiles allow more participants.",
    "How many cards are dealt face-up in the initial Solitaire (Klondike) layout?": "In the initial Klondike Solitaire layout, 7 cards are dealt face-up, one atop each of the seven tableau columns. The first column has one card (face-up), the second has two cards (one face-down and one face-up), and so on, with the seventh column having six face-down cards and one face-up card. A total of 28 cards are used in the tableau, with the remaining 24 forming the stock pile.",
    "How many possible first moves exist in Checkers?": "There are 7 possible first moves in standard Checkers (also known as English Draughts). Since pieces can only move diagonally forward on dark squares, and the initial setup places pieces on rows 1-3, only four pieces in the front row can move, with some having two possible moves. Checkers has been played for thousands of years and was solved by computer in 2007, proving that perfect play by both sides results in a draw.",
    "How many legal positions exist on a standard tic-tac-toe board?": "There are 5478 legal positions on a standard tic-tac-toe board when counting all valid board states that can arise during play. This number includes both terminal and non-terminal positions. The total number of possible games is 255,168, though many of these are strategically equivalent due to symmetry. Tic-tac-toe is a solved game, guaranteed to end in a draw with optimal play from both sides.",
    "How many different Tetris piece shapes (tetrominoes) are there?": "There are 7 different Tetris piece shapes, known as tetrominoes, each consisting of four connected squares. The pieces are commonly designated by the letters they resemble: I, O, T, S, Z, L, and J. The I-piece is the only one that can clear four lines simultaneously (called a Tetris), making it the most sought-after piece in competitive play.",
    "How many tiles are in a standard Azul game?": "A standard Azul game includes 100 tiles distributed equally among five colors, with 20 tiles per color. Players take turns drafting colored tiles from shared factory displays and placing them on their personal pattern boards. The game was designed by Michael Kiesling and won the prestigious Spiel des Jahres award in 2018.",
    "How many train cards does each player start with in Ticket to Ride?": "Each player starts with 4 train cards in Ticket to Ride, drawn from a deck of 110 cards. The deck consists of cards in eight different colors plus locomotive wild cards. Players collect and spend train cards to claim railway routes on the map, connecting cities to fulfill their destination ticket objectives for points.",
    "How many development cards are in the base Settlers of Catan?": "The base game of Settlers of Catan contains 25 development cards in total. These consist of 14 Knights, 5 Victory Point cards, 2 Road Building cards, 2 Year of Plenty cards, and 2 Monopoly cards. Development cards are purchased with one ore, one wool, and one grain, and must generally be held for at least one turn before being played.",
    "How many knight cards are in the base Settlers of Catan?": "The base Settlers of Catan contains 14 Knight cards in the development card deck. Playing a Knight allows the active player to move the robber to a different hex tile and steal one random resource card from any player with a settlement or city adjacent to that hex. The player who has played the most Knights (minimum three) holds the Largest Army card worth 2 victory points.",
    "How many harbor types are in the base Settlers of Catan?": "The base Settlers of Catan has 5 harbor types: one generic type and four resource-specific types. The generic harbors allow 3-for-1 trading of any single resource, while each specialized harbor offers 2-for-1 trading of its designated resource. Building a settlement on a harbor provides a permanent trading advantage that can significantly influence a player's strategy.",
    "How many plague cubes of each color start in the box in Pandemic?": "Pandemic starts with 24 plague cubes of each of the four colors (blue, yellow, black, and red) in the box, for a total of 96 cubes. During setup, cubes are placed on the board based on drawn infection cards, and more cubes are added each turn as diseases spread. If all 24 cubes of any one color are ever needed but unavailable, the players immediately lose the game.",
    "How many action points does each player get per turn in Pandemic?": "Each player gets 4 action points per turn in Pandemic, which can be spent on moving between cities, treating diseases, sharing knowledge cards, building research stations, or discovering cures. Players must strategize carefully to use their limited actions effectively. After performing four actions, the player draws two player cards and then draws infection cards that spread disease on the board.",
    "How many total letter tiles are in a standard Words With Friends game?": "A standard Words With Friends game uses 104 letter tiles in total, including 2 blank tiles that can represent any letter. The tile distribution differs slightly from Scrabble, with different quantities and point values for some letters. For example, Words With Friends assigns higher values to certain common letters and features a 15x15 board with a different bonus square layout.",
    "How many bonus squares are on a Words With Friends board?": "A Words With Friends board features 92 bonus squares spread across its 15x15 grid. These include double-letter, triple-letter, double-word, and triple-word score squares. The layout of bonus squares differs significantly from Scrabble, with the triple-word squares positioned differently and bonus squares placed more frequently throughout the center of the board.",
    "How many spaces are on a standard Trivial Pursuit board?": "A standard Trivial Pursuit board has 73 spaces arranged in a wheel-and-spoke pattern. The outer ring connects to the center hub through six spokes, with category headquarters positioned at the intersections. Players move around the board answering questions in six categories to collect colored wedges for their playing piece, then must answer a final question at the hub to win.",
    "How many category colors are in standard Trivial Pursuit?": "Standard Trivial Pursuit features 6 category colors: blue (Geography), pink (Entertainment), yellow (History), brown (Art & Literature), green (Science & Nature), and orange (Sports & Leisure). Players must collect a wedge in each of the six categories by correctly answering questions when landing on category headquarters. The categories have remained largely consistent since the game's creation in 1979.",
    "How many life tiles are in a standard Game of Life?": "The standard Game of Life includes 18 Life tiles that represent major life accomplishments and events. Players collect Life tiles by landing on certain spaces or achieving specific milestones during the game. At the end of the game, Life tiles are revealed and their values are added to each player's total cash to determine the winner.",
    "How many weapon cards are in the board game Clue?": "The board game Clue contains 6 weapon cards, each representing a different murder weapon: the candlestick, knife, lead pipe, revolver, rope, and wrench. At the start of each game, one weapon card is randomly placed in the confidential case file along with one suspect card and one room card. Players must deduce which weapon was used through the process of elimination.",
    "How many total cards are in a standard Clue game?": "A standard Clue game contains 21 cards in total: 6 suspect cards, 6 weapon cards, and 9 room cards. At the beginning of each game, one card from each category is randomly placed in the confidential case file to form the solution. The remaining 18 cards are dealt evenly among the players, who use deduction to determine the three hidden cards.",
    "How many ships does each player have in standard Battleship?": "Each player has 5 ships in standard Battleship: the Carrier (5 holes), Battleship (4 holes), Cruiser (3 holes), Submarine (3 holes), and Destroyer (2 holes). Players secretly place their ships on a 10x10 grid, then take turns calling out coordinates to try to hit and sink their opponent's fleet. The first player to sink all five of the opponent's ships wins.",
    "How many grid squares are on each Battleship board?": "Each Battleship board consists of 100 grid squares arranged in a 10x10 layout, with columns labeled A through J and rows numbered 1 through 10. Players have two grids: one for placing their own ships and one for tracking their shots against the opponent. The game requires strategic guessing and pattern recognition to efficiently locate and destroy all enemy ships.",
    "How many property spaces does Monopoly have (not including railroads and utilities)?": "Monopoly has 22 property spaces on its board, not including the 4 railroad spaces and 2 utility spaces. These 22 properties are organized into 8 color groups, ranging from the inexpensive brown (Mediterranean and Baltic) to the premium dark blue (Park Place and Boardwalk). Players can build houses and hotels on properties once they own all properties in a color group.",
    "How many utility spaces are on a Monopoly board?": "A Monopoly board has 2 utility spaces: Electric Company and Water Works. Each utility costs $150 to purchase. The rent for utilities is determined by dice rolls: if a player owns one utility, the rent is 4 times the dice roll, and if they own both utilities, the rent increases to 10 times the dice roll.",
    "How many total spaces does a player pass on one trip around the Monopoly board?": "A player passes 40 total spaces on one complete trip around the Monopoly board, returning to the Go square where they started. These spaces include 28 properties, 4 railroads, 2 utilities, and several special squares such as Chance, Community Chest, Income Tax, Luxury Tax, and the corner spaces (Go, Jail, Free Parking, and Go To Jail).",
    "How many resource cards can a player hold without discarding in Catan when a 7 is rolled?": "A player can hold up to 7 resource cards without discarding when a 7 is rolled in Settlers of Catan. Any player with more than 7 resource cards must discard half their hand (rounded down) when a 7 appears on the dice. This rule is designed to discourage hoarding resources and adds a risk-management element to the game.",
    "How many points does a settlement earn in Settlers of Catan?": "A settlement earns 1 victory point in Settlers of Catan. Settlements are the primary means of expanding across the board and collecting resources. Each settlement must be placed at a board intersection with at least two empty intersections between it and any other settlement or city, following the distance rule that prevents overcrowding.",
    "How many points does a city earn in Settlers of Catan?": "A city earns 2 victory points in Settlers of Catan, replacing a settlement that was previously worth 1 point and adding a net gain of 1 victory point. Cities also double resource production from adjacent hexes compared to settlements. Upgrading a settlement to a city requires 3 ore and 2 grain, making these resources particularly valuable in the late game.",
    "How many cards are in a standard Skip-Bo deck?": "A standard Skip-Bo deck contains 162 cards: 144 numbered cards (twelve each of the numbers 1 through 12) and 18 Skip-Bo wild cards. Each player receives a personal stockpile of 30 cards and the goal is to be the first to play all cards from the stockpile. Skip-Bo was created in 1967 and acquired by Mattel, who now publishes the game alongside Uno.",
    "How many cards are in a standard Phase 10 deck?": "A standard Phase 10 deck contains 108 cards, consisting of 96 numbered cards (two each of numbers 1 through 12 in four colors), 8 Wild cards, and 4 Skip cards. Players must complete ten specific phases in order, such as sets of matching numbers and runs of consecutive numbers. The game was created in 1982 and is published by Mattel.",
    "How many different phases must be completed to win Phase 10?": "A player must complete 10 different phases to win Phase 10, progressing through each phase in sequential order. The phases range from simple objectives like two sets of three to more challenging goals like a run of nine consecutive numbers. A player must successfully lay down the required combination during a hand to advance to the next phase.",
    "How many tiles are in a standard Rummikub set?": "A standard Rummikub set contains 106 tiles in total: 104 numbered tiles arranged in two sets of numbers 1 through 13 in each of four colors (black, blue, orange, and red), plus 2 joker tiles. Players draw tiles from a pool and arrange them on the table in valid runs and groups. Rummikub combines elements of the card game Rummy with tile-based gameplay.",
    "How many numbered tiles of each color are in Rummikub?": "Rummikub contains 26 numbered tiles of each color, consisting of two complete sets of tiles numbered 1 through 13. The four colors used are black, blue, orange, and red. Having duplicate tiles in each color allows for more complex combinations and strategies during gameplay, as players can use matching tiles to form groups of the same number in different colors.",
}

HARD_PARAGRAPHS = {
    "How many cards are in a Zephyr deck?": "A Zephyr deck contains 72 cards divided into four elemental suits of 18 cards each: Wind, Storm, Gale, and Calm. Each suit includes numbered cards from 1 to 12 and six special action cards. The game emphasizes hand management and timing, with players trying to play all their cards before opponents by matching elements or numbers.",
    "How many tiles are in a Stormhaven tile set?": "A Stormhaven tile set includes 96 tiles representing different terrain types such as rocky shores, deep waters, harbors, and storm zones. Players build the game board collaboratively by placing tiles each turn, creating a unique island map for every session. The variable board ensures high replayability and encourages adaptive strategy.",
    "How many pieces does each player start with in Ironforge?": "Each player starts with 22 pieces in Ironforge, comprising 10 infantry, 6 cavalry, 4 siege engines, and 2 commanders. The game simulates medieval fortress warfare, with players deploying their forces across a modular castle board. Commanders have special abilities that can turn the tide of battle when positioned strategically.",
    "How many hexes are on a standard Duskfall board?": "A standard Duskfall board consists of 127 hexes arranged in a circular pattern representing a post-apocalyptic wasteland. The hexes include resource zones, radiation fields, safe havens, and contested territories. Players explore the map by revealing face-down hex tiles, encountering threats and opportunities as they expand their settlements.",
    "How many resource types exist in Crystalheim?": "Crystalheim features 8 resource types: fire crystal, ice shard, thunder stone, shadow essence, light prism, earth core, water pearl, and void fragment. Players collect resources by controlling territory hexes that produce specific crystal types. Combining resources in specific patterns allows players to construct powerful structures and summon elemental guardians.",
    "How many action cards are in a Voidrunner deck?": "A Voidrunner deck contains 45 action cards that represent piloting maneuvers, weapon systems, and shield configurations for spaceship combat. The cards are divided into three categories: offensive (15 cards), defensive (15 cards), and tactical (15 cards). Players build custom decks from the full set before each match, choosing a strategy that suits their play style.",
    "How many sectors are on a standard Nebula Drift board?": "A standard Nebula Drift board features 36 sectors arranged in a 6 by 6 grid, each representing a region of space with unique properties. Sectors can contain asteroid fields, nebula clouds, space stations, wormholes, or empty void. Players navigate their fleets through the sectors, competing to control valuable trade routes and resource-rich regions.",
    "How many character classes are in Shadowpact?": "Shadowpact includes 14 character classes, each with a unique set of abilities and a distinct role in the cooperative dungeon-crawling experience. Classes range from frontline warriors like the Ironclad and Berserker to support roles like the Mystic Healer and Shadow Weaver. Players select their class at the start of each campaign and can unlock advanced abilities as they progress.",
    "How many dice are used in a round of Thunderstone?": "Each round of Thunderstone uses 7 dice: five standard six-sided dice and two special thunder dice that feature unique symbols including lightning bolts, shields, and critical strike markers. Players roll all seven dice simultaneously and then allocate results to different actions. The thunder dice add an element of unpredictability that can dramatically shift the outcome of encounters.",
    "How many victory points are needed to win Moonrise?": "A player needs 25 victory points to win Moonrise, a competitive territory control game set on a colonized lunar surface. Points are earned by establishing bases, completing research objectives, controlling resource deposits, and fulfilling secret mission cards. The first player to reach 25 points triggers the final round, giving other players one last chance to surpass them.",
    "How many terrain types are in Frostpeak Conquest?": "Frostpeak Conquest features 11 terrain types: tundra, glacier, frozen lake, snowfield, mountain peak, ice cave, hot spring, alpine forest, rocky outcrop, crevasse, and aurora zone. Each terrain type affects movement speed, combat bonuses, and resource availability differently. Controlling diverse terrain types is essential for a balanced strategy.",
    "How many spell cards are in the base Arcane Duel set?": "The base Arcane Duel set contains 60 spell cards distributed across five schools of magic: fire (12 cards), water (12 cards), earth (12 cards), air (12 cards), and arcane (12 cards). Each school has its own play style, with fire focusing on direct damage, water on healing and defense, and arcane on card manipulation. Players construct decks by combining spells from up to three schools.",
    "How many guild tokens are in a Tradecraft starting set?": "A Tradecraft starting set includes 18 guild tokens representing different merchant guilds that players can recruit to enhance their trading capabilities. Each guild token provides a unique bonus such as reduced shipping costs, access to exclusive markets, or protection from pirate raids. Players compete to recruit the most valuable guild combinations.",
    "How many islands are on a standard Tidalwave board?": "A standard Tidalwave board features 9 islands connected by sea routes that shift as tidal cards are played throughout the game. Each island produces different resources and offers unique building opportunities. The dynamic water levels created by tidal shifts mean that some routes become navigable while others are cut off, forcing players to constantly adapt their strategies.",
    "How many crew members does each player start with in Corsair's Gambit?": "Each player starts with 12 crew members in Corsair's Gambit, distributed among roles including navigator, gunner, lookout, and deckhand. Crew members can be assigned to different stations on the player's ship to improve specific capabilities like speed, firepower, or cargo capacity. Losing crew members in combat weakens the ship until replacements can be recruited at port.",
    "How many rounds are in a standard Dragonscale match?": "A standard Dragonscale match consists of 5 rounds, with each round representing a season in the dragon-taming calendar. During each round, players draft dragon eggs, train their hatchlings, and compete in aerial combat tournaments. Points accumulate across all five rounds, and the player with the highest total score at the end of the final round wins.",
    "How many trap cards are in the Labyrinth of Echoes base set?": "The Labyrinth of Echoes base set contains 30 trap cards that are shuffled into the dungeon deck and revealed as players explore the labyrinth. Trap types range from simple pit falls and poison darts to complex magical snares that affect the entire party. Players can attempt to disarm traps using their characters' skills, with failure resulting in damage or other penalties.",
    "How many upgrade slots does each ship have in Starfall Armada?": "Each ship in Starfall Armada has 6 upgrade slots that can be fitted with weapons, shields, engines, sensors, cargo modules, or special equipment. The slots are divided into three categories: two weapon mounts, two utility bays, and two core systems. Players customize their fleet by choosing upgrades that complement their overall battle strategy.",
    "How many event cards are in the Plague Chronicles deck?": "The Plague Chronicles deck contains 40 event cards that drive the narrative and introduce challenges throughout the cooperative survival game. Events include disease outbreaks, supply shortages, refugee crises, bandit attacks, and rare moments of hope like discovering a cache of medicine. Players draw one event card each round and must collectively decide how to respond.",
    "How many provinces are contested in the Warpath campaign map?": "The Warpath campaign map features 16 contested provinces arranged across a continental landmass divided by rivers and mountain ranges. Each province provides strategic advantages such as resource production, defensive terrain, or access to trade routes. Players begin with control of one home province and expand by conquering adjacent territories through military campaigns and diplomatic negotiations.",
    "How many minion tokens are in a Darkspire Dungeon starting set?": "A Darkspire Dungeon starting set includes 48 minion tokens representing the various creatures and monsters that inhabit the dungeon. Minion types include skeletons, goblins, shadow wraiths, cave trolls, and the dreaded darkspire guardians. The dungeon master player deploys these tokens to oppose the hero players as they delve deeper into the dungeon.",
    "How many power gems does each player begin with in Runebind?": "Each player begins with 3 power gems in Runebind, which serve as the primary resource for casting rune spells and activating magical effects. Power gems regenerate at the start of each turn, and players can increase their maximum gem capacity by controlling specific board locations. Managing gem expenditure is the central strategic challenge of the game.",
    "How many sanctuary tiles are on a Pilgrimage of Ash board?": "A Pilgrimage of Ash board contains 7 sanctuary tiles positioned at key intersections along the pilgrimage route. Sanctuaries provide healing, equipment upgrades, and quest completion opportunities for weary travelers. Reaching a sanctuary also allows players to save their progress and recruit new companions for the difficult journey ahead.",
    "How many trade routes are in the base Merchant Winds set?": "The base Merchant Winds set includes 20 trade routes connecting the game's various port cities across a network of sea lanes. Each trade route has a distance value, danger rating, and list of goods that can be profitably transported along it. Players compete to establish the most lucrative trading network by claiming routes and fulfilling delivery contracts.",
    "How many relic cards are in the Tomb of Eternity expansion?": "The Tomb of Eternity expansion includes 33 relic cards that represent ancient artifacts discovered in the depths of the tomb. Each relic grants unique powers ranging from combat bonuses to special movement abilities and puzzle-solving aids. Relics are found by successfully completing tomb chambers, and players must decide which relics to keep given their limited inventory slots.",
    "How many garrison slots are in each fortress in Siege of Ironhold?": "Each fortress in Siege of Ironhold has 4 garrison slots where players can station different unit types to defend against attacking armies. The slots are designated as wall, tower, gate, and keep, each providing different defensive bonuses to the units stationed there. Strategic placement of limited troops across these slots is key to surviving prolonged sieges.",
    "How many artifact tokens are in the base Mythfall collection?": "The base Mythfall collection contains 15 artifact tokens scattered across the game map at the start of each session. Artifacts grant powerful one-time abilities or permanent stat bonuses to the heroes who collect them. Some artifacts are guarded by mythical creatures that must be defeated before the artifact can be claimed.",
    "How many weather cards are in the Storm Cycle deck?": "The Storm Cycle deck contains 28 weather cards that determine environmental conditions each round, affecting movement, combat, and resource gathering for all players. Weather types include clear skies, light rain, heavy storm, blizzard, fog, drought, and hurricane. Players must plan their actions with weather forecasts in mind, as certain strategies become impossible during severe conditions.",
    "How many settlement tiles are in the Frontier Dawn box?": "The Frontier Dawn box includes 24 settlement tiles representing different frontier buildings such as homesteads, trading posts, mills, saloons, sheriff offices, and general stores. Players place settlement tiles to develop their frontier town, with each building providing specific benefits. The spatial arrangement of buildings matters, as adjacent structures can create synergy bonuses.",
    "How many quest cards are in the Wyrmwood Adventures starter?": "The Wyrmwood Adventures starter set contains 50 quest cards organized into five difficulty tiers of 10 quests each. Quests range from simple fetch missions and monster hunts to complex multi-part story arcs involving mystery solving and diplomatic negotiations. Completing quests earns experience points and loot that help heroes prepare for the increasingly dangerous challenges ahead.",
    "How many fleet cards does each player start with in Aether Seas?": "Each player starts with 8 fleet cards in Aether Seas, representing their initial armada of sky ships that sail through floating island archipelagos. The starting fleet includes two frigates, two corvettes, two cargo vessels, one flagship, and one scout. Players can expand their fleet by constructing new ships at controlled sky docks throughout the game.",
    "How many dungeon levels are in the Crypts of Malachar base set?": "The Crypts of Malachar base set features 10 dungeon levels of increasing difficulty, with each level containing unique room layouts, monster encounters, and treasure hoards. Players must clear each level before descending to the next, facing a powerful boss monster at every fifth level. The final level culminates in a confrontation with the lich king Malachar himself.",
    "How many hero cards are in the Champions of Eldoria deck?": "The Champions of Eldoria deck contains 36 hero cards representing warriors, mages, rogues, and clerics from six different kingdoms. Each kingdom contributes six heroes with complementary abilities designed to work together. Players draft heroes to form their adventuring party, and the synergy between chosen champions determines the effectiveness of the team.",
    "How many biome types are in the Terraform Genesis board?": "The Terraform Genesis board features 9 biome types: ocean, desert, forest, mountain, grassland, tundra, volcanic, swamp, and crystal canyon. Players compete to terraform a barren planet by converting neutral hexes into habitable biomes. Each biome type requires different resources to establish and provides distinct benefits once terraformed.",
    "How many outpost tokens are in the Void Frontier base set?": "The Void Frontier base set includes 21 outpost tokens that players deploy on the star map to establish their presence in unexplored space. Outposts serve as supply points, early warning stations, and staging areas for fleet operations. Each player begins with three outpost tokens and can manufacture additional ones at their home base using collected resources.",
    "How many council seats are contested in the Intrigue of Ravenmoor?": "The Intrigue of Ravenmoor features 13 council seats that players compete to fill with their loyal supporters through a combination of political maneuvering, bribery, and strategic alliances. Each council seat controls a different aspect of city governance, such as the treasury, the guard, the trade commission, or the judiciary. The player who controls the most seats at the end of five rounds wins.",
    "How many mutation cards are in the Genome Wars deck?": "The Genome Wars deck contains 44 mutation cards representing genetic modifications that players can apply to their creature armies. Mutations include enhanced strength, venomous attacks, armored plating, camouflage, flight capability, and regeneration. Players combine mutations to create unique creature variants, with some combinations producing powerful synergies and others creating unstable organisms.",
    "How many sectors are in the Hyperdrive Conflict galaxy map?": "The Hyperdrive Conflict galaxy map is divided into 42 sectors arranged in a spiral pattern radiating outward from the galactic core. Each sector contains star systems with varying strategic value, from resource-rich mining colonies to military strongholds and research facilities. Players expand their empires by claiming adjacent sectors and defending them from rival factions.",
    "How many tribe tokens are in the Dawn of Tribes starter?": "The Dawn of Tribes starter includes 30 tribe tokens representing the population units that players manage throughout the civilization-building game. Tribes can be assigned to gathering food, constructing buildings, training warriors, or exploring unknown territories. Managing the allocation of limited tribe tokens between these competing priorities is the core strategic challenge.",
    "How many blueprint cards are in the Factory Floor base set?": "The Factory Floor base set contains 55 blueprint cards representing different machines, conveyor systems, and production modules that players can construct in their factories. Each blueprint specifies input resources, output products, space requirements, and energy consumption. Players compete to design the most efficient production lines by combining blueprints in clever configurations.",
    "How many crew roles exist in the Starship Enigma game?": "The Starship Enigma game features 11 crew roles: captain, pilot, navigator, engineer, weapons officer, communications officer, science officer, medical officer, security chief, cargo master, and diplomatic envoy. Each role has unique abilities that contribute to the ship's overall effectiveness. In cooperative mode, players must coordinate their roles to handle the various crises that arise during interstellar voyages.",
    "How many treasure cards are in the Pirate's Bounty deck?": "The Pirate's Bounty deck contains 38 treasure cards representing different valuables that pirates can plunder from merchant ships and coastal towns. Treasures range from gold doubloons and silver bars to rare spices, exotic gems, ancient maps, and cursed artifacts. Each treasure has a point value, but cursed items impose penalties if a player holds too many at the end of the game.",
    "How many rune stones does each player start with in Runecaster?": "Each player starts with 8 rune stones in Runecaster, drawn randomly from a bag containing stones inscribed with ancient symbols. Players cast rune stones onto the game board, with their landing positions and orientations determining the magical effects produced. Skilled players learn to control their throws to consistently produce desired spell patterns.",
    "How many elemental cards are in the Primal Surge deck?": "The Primal Surge deck contains 64 elemental cards divided equally among four primal elements: 16 fire cards, 16 water cards, 16 earth cards, and 16 air cards. Each element has its own attack patterns, defensive capabilities, and combo potential. Players build decks by selecting cards from two or more elements, creating hybrid strategies that can catch opponents off guard.",
    "How many chapters are in a standard Mythos Unraveled campaign?": "A standard Mythos Unraveled campaign consists of 12 chapters, each presenting a self-contained mystery that connects to the overarching narrative of eldritch horror threatening a 1920s coastal town. Each chapter takes approximately two to three hours to play and introduces new locations, characters, and supernatural threats. Players' choices in earlier chapters affect the options available in later ones.",
    "How many mana crystals does each player begin with in Arcane Duels?": "Each player begins with 4 mana crystals in Arcane Duels, which are spent to cast spells and summon creatures during their turn. Players gain one additional mana crystal at the start of each turn, up to a maximum of ten. The escalating mana supply means that early turns feature small skirmishes while late-game turns see powerful spells and legendary creatures entering the battlefield.",
    "How many tiles make up the Echoing Caverns dungeon board?": "The Echoing Caverns dungeon board is composed of 81 tiles arranged in a 9 by 9 grid, with each tile representing a different cavern chamber. Tiles include crystal grottos, underground rivers, mushroom forests, bat colonies, and the lair of the cave dragon at the center. The board is assembled randomly at the start of each game, ensuring a unique dungeon layout every time.",
    "How many faction cards are in the Warfront Allegiance set?": "The Warfront Allegiance set contains 50 faction cards representing five competing military powers of 10 cards each. Each faction has a distinct combat philosophy: the Iron Legion emphasizes defense, the Storm Riders focus on mobility, the Shadow Guild uses stealth and sabotage, the Flame Order employs devastating attacks, and the Tide Compact controls the seas.",
    "How many dice are used in a round of Dragon's Gambit?": "Each round of Dragon's Gambit uses 8 dice: six standard twelve-sided dice and two special dragon dice featuring unique symbols such as fire breath, wing gust, tail sweep, and dragon roar. Players roll their dice pool and assign results to attack, defend, or activate special dragon abilities. The dragon dice can produce spectacular effects that dramatically alter the course of battle.",
    "How many supply tokens are in the Frontier Settlement starting kit?": "The Frontier Settlement starting kit contains 24 supply tokens representing essential resources like food, water, timber, and tools needed to establish a new colony. Players distribute supply tokens among their settlement buildings and expedition parties, balancing the needs of a growing population with the demands of exploration. Running out of supplies triggers crisis events that can devastate an unprepared settlement.",
    "How many hex tiles form the standard Nebula Conquest board?": "The standard Nebula Conquest board is formed by 37 hex tiles arranged in a honeycomb pattern, with each hex representing a stellar system or deep space region. The board is modular, with tile placement varying each game based on scenario cards. Central hexes tend to be resource-rich but heavily contested, while outer hexes offer safer but less rewarding positions.",
    "How many character abilities does each hero have in Shadow Legends?": "Each hero in Shadow Legends has 5 character abilities that define their role in the adventuring party. Abilities are categorized as one passive trait, two active combat skills, one utility skill, and one ultimate ability that charges over multiple turns. Players can customize their heroes by selecting ability upgrades at key story milestones.",
    "How many quest cards are in the Wanderer's Path base set?": "The Wanderer's Path base set contains 45 quest cards organized into three difficulty categories: 15 novice quests, 15 journeyman quests, and 15 master quests. Each quest describes an objective, potential rewards, and possible complications that may arise during completion. Players choose which quests to pursue based on their characters' strengths and current equipment.",
    "How many gold coins does each player begin with in Merchant Prince?": "Each player begins with 15 gold coins in Merchant Prince, representing their starting capital for building a commercial empire across the Mediterranean trade network. Gold is spent on purchasing goods, hiring ships, bribing officials, and establishing trading posts in foreign ports. Successful trades generate profit, while poor investments or pirate attacks can quickly deplete a player's reserves.",
    "How many artifact slots does each explorer have in Tomb Raiders?": "Each explorer in Tomb Raiders has 4 artifact slots in their inventory, limiting the number of ancient relics they can carry at any time. Players must make difficult choices about which artifacts to keep and which to leave behind when their slots are full. Artifacts provide various bonuses including enhanced combat abilities, puzzle-solving tools, and protection against tomb curses.",
    "How many biome tiles are in the standard Terraform Genesis set?": "The standard Terraform Genesis set includes 28 biome tiles that players place on the planetary grid during the terraforming process. Each biome tile is double-sided, with one side showing a barren landscape and the other showing a terraformed environment. Players flip tiles from barren to terraformed by spending the required resources, gradually transforming the planet into a habitable world.",
    "How many action tokens does each player receive per round in Chrono Clash?": "Each player receives 6 action tokens per round in Chrono Clash, which can be spent on movement, combat, time manipulation, and resource gathering. The time manipulation mechanic allows players to spend extra tokens to undo actions or peek at future event cards. Efficient use of the limited action tokens is crucial, as unused tokens do not carry over between rounds.",
    "How many city tiles are in the Metropolis Builder starting pack?": "The Metropolis Builder starting pack contains 32 city tiles representing different urban zones including residential blocks, commercial districts, industrial areas, parks, transportation hubs, and civic buildings. Players place tiles on a shared city grid, earning points for efficient urban planning and creating neighborhoods with compatible adjacent zones. Penalties apply for placing incompatible zones next to each other.",
    "How many spell components are in the Alchemy Wars base set?": "The Alchemy Wars base set includes 72 spell components divided into six ingredient types of 12 components each: herbs, minerals, essences, crystals, powders, and elixirs. Players collect components through exploration and trading, then combine them using recipe cards to create potions, bombs, enchantments, and transmutations. The vast number of possible combinations encourages creative experimentation.",
    "How many scouts does each player deploy in Recon Strike?": "Each player deploys 10 scouts at the start of Recon Strike, positioning them across the battlefield map to gather intelligence on enemy positions. Scouts have limited combat capability but provide crucial information about terrain, enemy movements, and hidden objectives. Losing scouts reduces a player's battlefield awareness, making them vulnerable to ambushes and surprise attacks.",
    "How many victory flags are contested in Battlefront Zero?": "Battlefront Zero features 7 victory flags positioned at strategic locations across the battlefield map. Players must capture and hold these flags to earn victory points each round. Flags closer to the center of the map are worth more points but are harder to defend due to their exposure. The game ends when one player accumulates a set number of victory points or eliminates all opposing forces.",
    "How many mission cards are in the Covert Ops deck?": "The Covert Ops deck contains 36 mission cards divided into four categories: infiltration (9 cards), extraction (9 cards), sabotage (9 cards), and intelligence (9 cards). Each mission specifies a target, difficulty level, required equipment, and potential complications. Players select missions based on their agents' specializations and available resources.",
    "How many weapon types exist in the Gladiator Arena game?": "The Gladiator Arena game features 9 weapon types: sword, spear, trident, net, axe, mace, bow, shield, and dual daggers. Each weapon type has distinct attributes for attack range, damage, speed, and special abilities. Players equip their gladiators before each bout, choosing weapons that complement their fighting style and counter their opponent's expected loadout.",
    "How many trade goods does each merchant start with in Silk Road Legends?": "Each merchant starts with 20 trade goods in Silk Road Legends, representing a diverse cargo of silk, spices, precious metals, ceramics, and other commodities valued along the ancient trade routes. Players move their caravans across the map, buying goods cheaply at production centers and selling them at premium prices in distant markets. Profits are reinvested in better camels, guards, and trade agreements.",
    "How many monster tokens are in the Nightmare Dungeon starting set?": "The Nightmare Dungeon starting set includes 56 monster tokens representing a bestiary of dungeon-dwelling creatures organized into seven monster families of eight tokens each. Monster families include undead, demons, beasts, constructs, aberrations, elementals, and the dungeon boss and its elite guards. The dungeon master distributes monster tokens across dungeon rooms according to encounter tables.",
    "How many starships does each fleet start with in Galactic Armada?": "Each fleet starts with 8 starships in Galactic Armada: two battleships, two cruisers, two destroyers, one carrier, and one command vessel. Players can construct additional ships at starbases using collected resources, but each ship type requires different materials and construction time. Fleet composition and formation are crucial tactical decisions that determine the outcome of space battles.",
    "How many terrain cards are in the Wilderness Survival deck?": "The Wilderness Survival deck contains 44 terrain cards representing the varied environments that players encounter during their journey through untamed wilderness. Terrain types include dense forest, open meadow, rocky ridge, river crossing, swamp, desert stretch, mountain pass, coastal cliff, and more. Each terrain card presents unique survival challenges and resource gathering opportunities.",
    "How many invention tokens are in the Age of Discovery set?": "The Age of Discovery set includes 18 invention tokens representing technological breakthroughs that advance a player's civilization. Inventions range from basic tools like the compass and printing press to advanced technologies like steam engines and telegraphs. Each invention provides immediate benefits and unlocks access to more advanced inventions further up the technology tree.",
    "How many alliance cards are in the Throne Wars expansion?": "The Throne Wars expansion contains 28 alliance cards representing political agreements, military pacts, and trade deals that players can forge with rival factions and neutral powers. Each alliance card specifies terms, benefits, and conditions under which the alliance can be broken. Strategic use of alliances can provide crucial advantages, but betraying an ally carries reputation penalties.",
    "How many minion types exist in the Overlord's Siege game?": "The Overlord's Siege game features 13 minion types that the overlord player can recruit and deploy against the hero players. Minion types include goblins, orcs, trolls, dark knights, shadow assassins, necromancers, fire imps, frost wraiths, stone golems, plague rats, bat swarms, spider broodlings, and the elite dragon guard. Each type has unique combat stats and special abilities.",
    "How many portal tiles are on the Riftwalk board?": "The Riftwalk board contains 6 portal tiles that connect different regions of the dimensional maze. Portals allow instant travel between distant parts of the board but require spending dimensional energy tokens to activate. Each portal leads to a fixed destination, and memorizing the portal network is essential for efficient movement through the rifts.",
    "How many harvest tokens are in the Farmstead Chronicles base set?": "The Farmstead Chronicles base set includes 40 harvest tokens representing crops and livestock produced on the player's farm throughout the growing seasons. Harvest tokens come in five types: grain (10), vegetables (8), fruit (8), dairy (7), and livestock (7). Players sell harvest tokens at the market for coins, with prices fluctuating based on supply and demand driven by event cards.",
}
